# Vulnerability details

## Vulnerability details
when user call `deposit()` protocol will call `_supplyAndBorrow()`
```solidity
    function _supplyAndBorrow(
        address assetIn,
        uint256 amountIn,
        address assetOut,
        uint256 borrowOut
    ) internal override virtual{
        _supply(assetIn, amount);
@>      aaveV3().setUserUseReserveAsCollateral(assetIn, true);
        aaveV3().borrow(assetOut, borrowOut, 2, 0, address(this));
    }

```
Each time the method is executed, `aaveV3().setUserUseReserveAsCollateral(true)` is called once. 
Its primary purpose is to set `assetIn` as collateral. 
However, if `assetIn` is already collateral, calling this method again will result in a revert.

https://github.com/aave/aave-protocol/blob/4b4545fb583fd4f400507b10f3c3114f45b8a037/contracts/lendingpool/LendingPool.sol#L782
```solidity
    function setUserUseReserveAsCollateral(address _reserve, bool _useAsCollateral)
        external
        nonReentrant
        onlyActiveReserve(_reserve)
        onlyUnfreezedReserve(_reserve)
    {
        uint256 underlyingBalance = core.getUserUnderlyingAssetBalance(_reserve, msg.sender);

        require(underlyingBalance > 0, "User does not have any liquidity deposited");

        require(
@>          dataProvider.balanceDecreaseAllowed(_reserve, msg.sender, underlyingBalance),
@>          "User deposit is already being used as collateral"
        );

        core.setUserUseReserveAsCollateral(_reserve, msg.sender, _useAsCollateral);

        if (_useAsCollateral) {
            emit ReserveUsedAsCollateralEnabled(_reserve, msg.sender);
        } else {
            emit ReserveUsedAsCollateralDisabled(_reserve, msg.sender);
        }
    }
```


## Impact

`deposit()` can only be executed once, subsequent execute will fail.

